WEBVTT

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.580
Huh?

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:56.560
Stay away.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.340
One more step, and you'll 
never be able to go back.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.520
Gripen.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.820
If you make too much contact 
with the Unphysical Layer,

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.550
your mind will be unable to maintain itself.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.760
The more time passes, the more 
indistinct your existence becomes.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.420
The Un... What?

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.500
Johari's Window is open.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.880
You fell through.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.140
Where are we?

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:27.890
The sea.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.150
The sea?

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.560
This is the only place where 
I can get my memories back.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.290
Memories?

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:38.640
What did you remember?

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.000
Everything.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.870
Even the reason you stabilize 
when you're with me?

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.510
I understand it.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.610
Why?

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.750
Because that's how I was made.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.460
Made? By who?

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.910
What? What did you say?

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.930
Then, um...

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.400
What are the Xi?

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.350
They are... hope.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.730
"Hope"?

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.900
In order to...

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.750
Hey! Gripen!

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.170
A dream?

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.660
Kei, the lunches are ready!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:06.470
<i>Unphysical Layer</i>

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.970
Are you ready to go?

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.970
I need to pack up the blanket.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.970
And the trash bags and towels...

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.470
Wake up already!

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.510
Sorry, I'm feeling groggy this morning.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.030
Did I have a weird dream, maybe?

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.120
I'll get the stuff ready!

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.490
You just get yourself ready!

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.010
But...

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.880
Just hurry up!

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.320
What great weather!

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.880
Come on, slow down.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.120
We can't have any fun if our day 
off is too jam-packed to breathe.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.770
But you never say you want 
to go to picnics and stuff...

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.480
And I've got this feeling 
that if I don't hurry,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.750
you're going to run off again.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.720
What?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.300
There's no reason for it.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.830
It's just a feeling.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.560
Sorry for being weird.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.320
Anyway, you're sure you don't 
have work today, right?

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.260
Yeah.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.290
<i>Well, unless the Xi attack.</i>

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:09.090
<i>But things on the continent have been 
calm ever since the attack on Umidori.</i>

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.840
Okay, off we go!

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.440
Let's have fun!

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.010
Get in. We need to talk.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.650
Um... we've got plans.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.270
We have important plans, too.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.200
And we need you.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:27.760
There's no time. Let's go.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.100
Wait!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:29.970
Hey!

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.610
Kei, you jerk!

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.360
Now what do I do?

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.710
Are you okay?

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.690
Whose fault do you think it is?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.940
Sorry, but this is important.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.220
Our negotiating partners kept their 
plans vague until the last second.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:47.740
This morning, they insisted 
on a rush meeting.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.910
"Negotiating partners"?

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.490
The US Military.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.090
I'll have them explain when we get there.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:58.740
If I tried to explain, it would 
probably just confuse you.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.450
So when will I be able to get home?

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.620
It'll be a while.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.850
It's going to take three hours 
just to get there and back.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.330
Three hours?

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.150
Where are we going?

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.730
Atsugi.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.480
<i>Atsugi Base</i>

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.390
It's been a while.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:25.560
Two years since we've met in person, I think.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.330
There was no real need for us to meet.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.880
Oh, I'll introduce you.

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:34.420
This is William Shankle from DARPA.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:37.280
He and I were grad students in the same lab.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.090
And now we both work for the military.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:41.730
DARPA?

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:45.210
The American Defense Advanced 
Research Projects Agency.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.240
An R&D lab for their military.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.930
Oh, you're the two man cell 
everybody talks about?

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.080
Welcome to Atsugi.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.840
An Anima?

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.950
You really are a normal human.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.640
You sure you haven't been modified anywhere?

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.670
No artificial arms or 
legs, or implanted chips?

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:15.640
No, I'm...

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.620
Rhino, that's rude.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.350
You need to introduce yourself 
before you start asking questions.

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:22.750
I told you that.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.290
Okay!

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:31.590
I'm F/A-18E-ANM Rhino, with 
the American Pacific fleet!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.010
We'll be going on the next mission together!

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.360
Nice to meet you.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.590
Mission?

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.600
You weren't told?

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:42.500
It was really sudden.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.740
I thought it would be better to share the 
information we have once everyone's together.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.140
Sheesh...

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:49.720
Lazy ass.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.070
Um, what mission?

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.200
The Shanghai Landing Mission.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.730
We're going to establish a beachhead on the 
continent to help launch a counterattack.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.590
Let me introduce myself properly.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:07.550
I'm William Shankle. My specialty is AI,

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.750
but at the moment, I'm researching 
Anima and Daughters.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.630
Rhino here is one of the things we've made.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.040
Oh, I'm Narutani Kei.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.430
And this is...

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:21.140
JAS39 ANM Gripen.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.960
I'm happy to meet you both.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:29.310
As we were just saying, we're planning 
an invasion of the continent.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:33.770
Taking back Shanghai?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:39.740
If we work with you Japanese 
Anima, we can do it.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.320
We're participating, too?

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.950
But...

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:45.830
But?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:51.190
In the last mission, we ran into 
an incredible number of Xi.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.440
At Umidori?

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:57.750
Yes. There were a hundred, 
no, two hundred there!

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:02.340
If we're attacking China itself, 
there'll be even more, right?

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:06.430
I see. So you're concerned we 
don't have enough firepower.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:10.540
You're right. The US is 
behind in Anima research.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:13.830
Our only success so far has been Rhino here.

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:18.590
But then even if we join you, 
that's only four or five Anima.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.440
We have a plan.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.920
A plan?

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:26.990
There are ways to deal with 
the Xi besides using Anima.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:11.220
The FQ-150A Brawler.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:14.900
An unmanned fighter 
developed to fight the Xi.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.380
An unmanned fighter?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.630
We analyzed the combat data 
from the Anima and Daughters,

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:22.340
turned it into software, and 
loaded it into the fighters.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:25.710
Twelve of them, a full squadron,

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.770
will be used in this operation.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.330
But if the Xi use their EPCM,

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:34.150
only Anima can hit them, right?

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:39.170
We've analyzed over 10 billion 
EPCM patterns and developed

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:42.040
an algorithm that can deal with it.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.440
The Brawler can identify the direction 
and intensity of the jamming,

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:49.790
and respond exactly as an 
Anima could in every manner.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.130
It can shoot them down?

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.490
I'm sure of it.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:59.040
You can't expect a crappy knock-off 
like that to work in a real battle.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.980
You had to use statistical analysis because 
you couldn't actually figure out

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.870
how EPCM works, right, Willy?

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:08.900
It's better than letting something 
as unscientific as an Anima

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.240
remain a black box while using it in combat!

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:16.330
Who was it who was begging 
me for my combat data?

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.960
Hey, let's get lunch.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.550
They're going to be a while.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.650
Without me, you never 
could've gotten this done.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:17.650
But...

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:24.900
I took what you and the Russians 
started and perfected it!

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.560
Yeah.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:26.220
Let's go.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:28.310
If we ever want something to fight 
the Xi with besides Anima...

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.910
Hurry, hurry.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.260
Let's go!

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:31.000
Your plan is to use these ugly knock-offs?

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:34.200
What do you think about 
those unmanned fighters?

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:35.810
I don't know.

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:38.640
I don't hear anything from them.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.750
They're as cold and silent as iron.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.790
They're not like Daughters?

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:47.330
No. It's hard to put it into words.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:49.680
Can they fight the Xi?

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.920
That's impossible.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.810
Their movements are simplistic, 
and their reaction time is slow.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:56.060
All they could do is try and dodge.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.070
I see...

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:01.010
But that changes if there's enough of them.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.310
Having any allies who can 
work under EPCM is valuable.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:09.070
Yashirodoori-san didn't seem to like them.

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:13.390
I think he doesn't like sending unmanned 
fighters up knowing they'll be shot down.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:15.990
Because it's not elegant?

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:20.990
Haruka sees no difference 
between humans and machines.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.490
If you think of the two as separate,

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:26.010
we Anima are also unmanned units.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.250
Which means we're expendable, too.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:30.760
I'm back!

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:34.650
I bought a little bit too much.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.890
A little bit too much?

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:40.090
Don't worry about it. It's my treat.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:42.200
That's not the issue.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.770
Kei, hurry.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.860
I am being forced to endure terribly!

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.420
Okay, let's eat.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:59.800
Hey, can I ask a question?

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:00.980
Wh-What?

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.950
How come she can only 
fly when she's with you?

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.840
Can you two feel each 
other when you're apart?

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.470
Are you, like, connected 
by a mysterious power?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.200
H-Hold on!

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.520
I don't really know myself.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.430
The JSDF is looking into it, but...

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.900
I see.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:20.540
Sorry.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.860
No, it's fine.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.640
Tell me about the other Anima, then.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.740
There're others besides Gripen, right?

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.440
Y-Yeah.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.150
One of them's really silly and loud.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.300
And one's really mean and sarcastic.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.750
Do I have a cold?

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.160
Don't worry.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.910
They say a certain type of 
person won't catch colds.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:48.300
What are Kei-san and Gripen doing 
at Atsugi right now, I wonder?

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.810
They might be eating a ton 
of food at a welcoming party!

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:52.550
I wish I could've gone!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.860
I'm so jealous.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.280
You've got lots of other Anima around you.

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.490
America isn't making any 
other Anima besides you?

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:04.280
Nope! We keep spending a 
ton of money and failing.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.110
The higher-ups are panicking, you know.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:11.430
If Japan and America fought, it 
would be four Anima against one.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:15.070
Eight versus one if Russia joined in.

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:17.250
War with Japan?

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:21.470
"Prepare for the worst" 
is the military's motto.

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:25.090
That's probably why they're making 
those cheap Brawler things.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.440
That's... But...

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.970
Humans are weird, huh?

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.710
They've got an enemy outside already,

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.720
and they're looking for an enemy inside.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.980
Hey, what do you think?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.520
We look like humans.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.750
Will the same thing ever happen to us?

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:47.440
Will we make groups, draw distinctions 
between friends and outsiders,

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.450
and look for things to fight each other over?

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:54.270
There you are.

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:55.160
I've been looking for you.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.280
Sorry. We were getting lunch.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.530
Narutani-kun, do you have 
some time after this?

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:02.720
Yeah.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:05.810
You too, Gripen, if possible.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:12.060
As I said earlier, AI is my specialty.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:16.090
And I've been wondering if it's possible to 
analyze the Xi's actions from that perspective.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.010
The Xi's actions?

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:20.480
It's impossible to analyze any single action,

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.300
but with millions or tens 
of millions of data points,

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:26.750
it should be possible to see 
what priorities drive them.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:27.990
Were you able to do it?

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.630
If only it were that easy.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:32.410
But...

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:35.510
I was able to make a simple simulation.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:37.110
It's a game, basically.

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:39.670
Blue are human military units.

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.100
Green are civilians.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.360
Red are the Xi.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.550
Once you're done moving, it's Red's turn.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:49.500
The CPU will select the appropriate response 
for the Xi to take based on your actions,

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.250
using the data it has on them.

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:54.070
The areas where civilians 
are gathered are cities.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.500
No other areas can hold 
large numbers of people,

00:15:56.500 --> 00:16:00.050
and as time passes, unit numbers 
outside cities decline.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:04.800
Humans can't survive for long periods of 
time without infrastructure, after all.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:08.150
Then I have to protect the cities, don't I?

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.300
That's one of the things 
we'd like to see how someone

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.820
who isn't part of the research team chooses.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:15.530
What do I do to win?

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.850
There are two ways. One 
is to wipe out the Xi.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:21.630
The second is to keep 
humanity alive for 10 years.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:26.070
If humanity's wiped out before 10 
years have passed, it's game over.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.580
Interested?

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.960
<i>Where do I start? I know...</i>

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:46.540
If I remember right, when 
the Xi first appeared,

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.470
none of the nations of the 
world really believed it.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:51.280
They didn't trust each other, and so 
their response was delayed, right?

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:54.210
They all thought it might actually 
be an army from another country.

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:57.280
If everybody had cooperated from the start...

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:00.290
Yes, that's a standard opening, but...

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.410
You need to keep in mind how 
much more powerful they are.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.650
It's impossible to beat 
the Xi with equal numbers.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.210
That's a loss.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:42.410
You lasted 30 turns. Two 
and a half years, I guess.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.390
Can I try again?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.500
As many times as you like.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:20.590
That's enough.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:25.330
All right, I guess it's your turn next.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.610
Me?

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:27.340
Yeah.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:29.210
I won't force you to, but...

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:30.700
Kei?

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:32.840
Go for it.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.210
Listen, you can't...

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.750
Shut up and watch.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:15.670
How?

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:18.690
The cities were annihilated. There's 
not a single military unit left.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:19.830
But...

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.870
Humanity survived.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:28.840
All you did was draw humanity 
away from the cities.

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:32.930
Into the mountains and forests, places 
it's hard to imagine humans surviving.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:36.180
What made you do that?

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:37.630
I don't know.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:40.570
I just felt it was better to do that.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.040
Felt?

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.570
Yes. Intuition.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.230
It just felt right that way.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:49.980
Intuition?

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:51.750
Is it Haruka's programming?

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.760
Or an effect of the machine learning?

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:55.340
Hey, Shankle-san!

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.340
Or something else...

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:59.180
I want to analyze your thought 
routines and memory area.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.450
You don't mind, right?

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:03.250
I won't hurt your personality data.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:05.170
Just a little... just a little!

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.320
Please!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.510
Shankle-san!

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:11.200
Yashirodoori-san?

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:12.910
We're leaving.

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:14.740
Okay...

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.290
Haruka!

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.920
What humanity needs is information!

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:25.440
If we just accept things as they 
are, we'll never move forward!

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:31.930
Willy, you don't understand 
what the Anima are.

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:43.450
Um, what did you mean back there?

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:46.310
About how he didn't understand
what the Anima are.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.380
Do you think it's possible to 
analyze a living creature's brain?

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:54.530
To perfectly explain every 
single action it takes?

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:57.290
I don't think so.

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:58.870
You're right.

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:00.670
The Xi's core is the same way.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.710
The minute you see them as computers,

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:04.500
you cease to be able to understand 
what they really are.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:10.660
That idiot Shankle sees 
Anima as simple programs.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.750
That's why he jumps to conclusions.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:17.120
He thinks that if we could read their source 
code, we could reveal their hidden mysteries.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:20.500
Do these things look that simple to you?

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:23.700
They have minds. They think.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.150
Which means they're not programs.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:29.120
We need to educate and speak to 
them and make them our allies.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.440
We need to be persistent, 
and spend the time it takes.

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:36.400
The Anima and Xi are different, right?

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.910
Of course!

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:39.140
What are you talking about?

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:52.850
<i>You're you... right?</i>

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.760
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:33.650
ALT 10: "The Mission to Retake Shanghai."

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>The Mission to Retake Shanghai</i>

00:23:34.170 --> 00:23:37.750
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
